            <ArticleTitle>Comparison of morphine slow release tablet (MST) and morphine sulphate solution (MSS) in the treatment of cancer pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>672-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A cross-over, single blind trial of MST and MSS in relieving pain of advanced cancer patients is described. Forty-nine cases completed the study. Both MST and MSS gave equally excellent pain relief in the patients as judged by the pain score of VAS and pain rating scale by a nurse, and the duration of sleep. The daily effective dose was 55.5 +/- 19.7 mg for MST and 61.0 +/- 11.0 mg of MSS.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
